# Netlify headers — awkale.me
#
# This file MUST end up in the publish directory (build/client) to take effect.
# Vite copies public/* to the output root, which is why it lives in public/ and
# not at the repo root. A root-level _headers is silently ignored.

# --- staging guard: REMOVE AT CUTOVER ----------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0002 puts the new site on a public *.netlify.app while awkale.me still
# serves the old one, and chose a sitewide noindex over password protection — the
# project has no password set, so this is the only thing stopping a staging copy
# of the whole archive being indexed as a duplicate of the real site.
#
# Delete this block at cutover, in the same change that adds the ALIAS. Leaving it
# in place ships a site nobody can find.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# --- Content-Security-Policy: sitewide, and it OUTLIVES the block above -------
#
# ADR-0010 wanted this so "no third-party client-side beacons" is a constraint the
# browser enforces rather than a convention the next edit can break silently.
#
# DELIBERATELY A SEPARATE /* BLOCK from the staging guard, which gets deleted at
# cutover. Netlify merges headers from every matching rule, so both apply — verified
# locally, because if only the first match won, deleting the staging block would take
# this with it, or this would suppress the noindex.
#
# `script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` — and the reasoning is amended into ADR-0010.
# The record chose `'sha256-…'` over the theme script believing there was ONE inline
# script. There are NINE per page, and React Router's route import map differs on
# every one, so a static hash list is impossible and a nonce needs a server that
# `ssr: false` does not have. `'self'` still blocks `<script src="…">` from any other
# origin, which is the property ADR-0010 actually wanted; what `'unsafe-inline'`
# gives up is hardening against INJECTED inline script, which needs attacker-
# controlled content.
#
# THAT LAST CLAUSE USED TO READ "and this site renders none — no user input, no
# query-param rendering, no remote HTML". AWK-55 made the middle third false:
# `/concerts/` now renders `?conductor=` and `?hall=` values, as facet tag text and
# in the `aria-label` of each tag's remove button. Both go through JSX, so React
# escapes them and they reach the DOM as text and never as markup — there is no
# injection here, and no change to the directives below. But the site is no longer
# in the category the original reasoning leaned on, so a future edit rendering a
# query parameter through `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, or into an inline `<script>`,
# would now have real reach. Check that before widening this.
#
# NOTE browsers IGNORE `'unsafe-inline'` when a hash or nonce is present, so never
# add one here expecting belt-and-braces.
#
# `style-src` needs it too, measured not assumed: 114 inline `style=` attributes in
# the built output, all React Aria's visually-hidden text.
#
# `img-src 'self'` with no `data:` — ADR-0013. Netlify Image CDN serves from this
# origin (`/.netlify/images`), so AWK-40 needs no change here.
#
# `form-action 'self'` — ADR-0011, and load-bearing: form-action has NO fallback to
# default-src, so without this line the policy would permit a POST to any origin.
#
# `connect-src` is intentionally absent; it falls back to default-src 'self'. A
# dynamic import counts as script, not connect, so the search index in AWK-41 needs
# nothing added.
#
# THAT IS WHY THE INDEX IS `/search-index.js` AND NOT `.json`. AWK-41 found the
# original plan unbuildable as recorded: `import()` of a `.json` URL requires import
# attributes (`with { type: 'json' }`), which is too new to rely on, and `fetch` is
# what ADR-0011 rejected to get this property in the first place. An ES module
# exporting the same array is script by definition. Do not "tidy" it back to JSON.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

# --- /contact/sent/ : noindex, permanently ------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0011. A real prerendered page with no inbound purpose — it exists only because
# a native POST has to land somewhere. It must never be indexed.
#
# THIS RULE IS CURRENTLY REDUNDANT AND MUST NOT BE DELETED FOR THAT REASON. The
# sitewide staging block above covers it incidentally today; removing that block at
# cutover is precisely what exposes this page. Landing the rule first, while it is
# still a no-op, is the only way it cannot be forgotten in the same edit that makes
# it necessary — which is the coupling AWK-44 exists to manage.
#
# Both spellings are listed deliberately. Netlify normalises trailing slashes when
# matching REDIRECTS; it is not documented as doing so for HEADERS, and the served
# canonical form here is slash-ful while the prerender enumerator is slash-free. Two
# lines cost nothing; a missed match costs an indexed page nobody wanted.
/contact/sent
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/contact/sent/
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# --- fonts --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted, content-hashed at build, so they can be cached hard. These are the
# latin-subset woff2 files in public/fonts — see that directory's README for the
# diacritics caveat before ADR-0007's IMSLP pass ships.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
